 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Geometric fibre of a finite morphism",
 "statement": "Let $h:W\\to V$ be a morphism and let $\\bar v:\\operatorname{Spec}\\Omega\\to V$ be a\ngeometric point with $\\Omega$ algebraically closed. The *geometric fibre* of $h$\nover $\\bar v$ is the set of morphisms $\\bar w:\\operatorname{Spec}\\Omega\\to W$ with\n$h\\circ\\bar w=\\bar v$; equivalently, the set of $\\Omega$-points of the scheme-theoretic\nfibre $W\\times_V\\operatorname{Spec}\\Omega$. It is finite when $h$ is finite.",
 "source": {
